> if you were to run an analysis specifying the estimator as "MLR" and missing as "fiml", would that be the appropriate way to employ the robust fiml approach to handling missing data?

Yes, assuming your data are continuous.  MLM only works for complete data (so listwise deletion), but MLR is an asymptotically equivalent correction that allows incomplete data.

