> Running this second model results in the error: "some variables have no values (only missings) or no variance." Are there better ways to incorporate a binary, time-varying predictor?

In order to be a predictor variable, it needs to be a variable.  All NA or all == values means it is nonexistent or a constant, respectively, implying there is no distinguishing between people who did/not receive an email on that occasion.  You can still include the time-varying covariates at other times, just leave the ones out that are not variables.

